# DTF tier manifest: conda-jlap-incremental  (artifact-keeper#4175, epic #4172)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single.
#
# THE BUG (1.11.x)
# #4175  a hosted subdir's JLAP was served only as repodata.json.jlap (conda
#        requests repodata.jlap and got 404), and it named only the current
#        index hash with no patches, so a JLAP client (conda
#        --experimental=jlap) downloaded the whole repodata.json.zst after
#        every channel change.
#
# THE FIX (1.12.0, artifact-keeper G5 PR3)
#        each revision of a subdir is recorded with its BLAKE2b-256 and an
#        RFC 6902 patch from the previous document is appended to a stored
#        JLAP; range requests from the client's saved position return the new
#        lines only.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   PUT    /conda/{hosted}/noarch/{file}         uploads (fixtures/conda/build.sh)
#   DELETE /conda/{hosted}/noarch/{file}         withdraw
#   a REAL conda 25.11 client (condaforge/miniforge3:25.11.0-1, the last line
#   that still implements JLAP) with --experimental=jlap and
#   local_repodata_ttl=0, talking to the backend through a logging reverse
#   proxy (fixtures/logproxy.py) in the backend's network namespace.
#
# Oracle (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1): see oracle.sh's header.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
